<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Wheat markets quiet.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Wheat markets quiet.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hard red winter wheat sales were light from Kansas to Texas Tuesday as farmers had sold most of their old-crop and did not appear willing to sell more of the new-crop, dealers said.</p>
<p>Oklahoma sources said rain Monday was beneficial to the crop. Ninety-five percent of the state's crop was headed, behind last year's 99 percent but on par with the five-year average, said the state's Agricultural Statistics Service.</p>
<p>Northwest Kansas remained dry, but dealers there said forecasts called for a 50 percent chance of showers late Tuesday or Wednesday.</p>
<p>Dry conditions have slowed wheat development and prevented sorghum planting, dealers said.</p>
